**length:** FIRST, "春风轻轻吹醒大地", has 8 characters (春风轻轻吹醒大地), not 6. SECOND, "春风吹醒大地", has exactly 6 and no punctuation.

**language:** Both replies are a single Chinese sentence, so both meet the language constraint.

**better_piece:** Both are coherent, vivid lines about spring. FIRST adds "轻轻", which is pleasant, but it breaks the explicit 6-character requirement. SECOND meets every requirement and is just as clear and imagistic, so it is the better piece for this instruction.

